{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST report a requirement or example with a missing closing fence or an empty body. Full names of `{req}` and `{example}` definitions MUST be unique across requirements, examples, and named definitions. Habeas MUST report every duplicate full name, including collisions involving named definitions, and identify both the duplicate declaration and the first declaration.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** The requirement is implemented and the tests cover its main cases.\n\n**Implementation** (`collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs`, fed by `definition_blocks` in `src/lib.rs`, and surfaced by `load_definitions`):\n- **Missing closing fence:**\n  - `definition_blocks` marks a block `closed = false` when it finds no closing colon fence. Such a block runs to the end of the file.\n  - `collect_definitions` then reports `<file>:<line>: <kind> <name> is missing a closing colon fence`.\n  - This applies to `req`, `example` and `definition` blocks.\n- **Empty body:** the body text is trimmed. If nothing is left, the error is `<kind> <name> has no text`.\n- **Duplicate full names:**\n  - All kinds share one `BTreeMap` keyed by the full name (namespace plus name). That covers requirements, examples and named definitions.\n  - On a collision it reports `<source>: duplicate <kind> <name>; first declared at <first source>`. This identifies both the duplicate declaration and the first one.\n  - Every duplicate is reported, because the loop continues after each error.\n- **Surfacing:** `load_definitions` joins all collected errors into one `InvalidData` error. `validate_repository` also reports them in `report.errors`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `reports_a_missing_closing_colon_fence` checks the exact message `md/requirements.md:1: requirement requirements.ready is missing a closing colon fence`.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks all three of these:\n  - a duplicate requirement, with the message `duplicate requirement requirements.one; first declared at md/requirements.md:3`;\n  - an empty requirement (`requirement requirements.empty has no text`);\n  - several other validation errors.\n- `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` covers these cases:\n  - a requirement and an example sharing a full name (`duplicate example rules.repeated; first declared at md/rules.md:1`);\n  - a duplicate example with the first declaration's line number;\n  - an empty example body;\n  - an unclosed example.\n- `tests/definitions.rs`, `invalid_declarations_and_reference_targets_are_reported`, covers:\n  - an unclosed `{definition}`;\n  - a requirement and a named definition colliding (`duplicate definition bad.x`).\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs`, `discovery_errors_fail_before_configuration_or_inference`, covers the end-to-end CLI case. An unclosed requirement makes `author --all` fail with the file location and the \"missing a closing colon fence\" diagnostic.\n\n**Minor gaps:**\n- The definition-collision test checks the \"duplicate definition bad.x\" text but not the \"first declared at\" suffix. The code path is the same one the other tests exercise.\n- An empty named definition body has no direct test. It uses the same empty-text check as requirements and examples.\n- I found no FIXME or TODO markers relating to this requirement.",
